1. Scope and definitions

"Licensor" means Hefesoft SAS, Colombia, to the extent it owns or is authorized
to license the relevant rights. "Software" means the Savia source code,
executables, and documentation distributed with this License, excluding
separately licensed third-party materials. "You" means the individual or legal
entity exercising rights under this License. When acting for an employer or
customer, that employer or customer must independently qualify under section 3.
"Modified Software" means changes to or derivative works of the Software.

"Monthly Revenue" means the total gross revenue of the relevant company from
all business activities worldwide during a calendar month, not merely revenue
generated using Savia. Revenue is measured before expenses and income taxes,
excluding sales taxes collected for authorities and deducting actual refunds
and credit notes. Revenue in another currency must be converted to United
States dollars using a consistently applied, publicly documented monthly
average exchange rate published by a central bank for that month. The company
must retain its calculation and the exchange-rate source. Internal departments
and branches of the same legal entity are not separate companies for this test.

2. Conditional grant

Subject to every condition of this License, Licensor grants You a worldwide,
non-exclusive, royalty-free copyright license to use, reproduce, study,
modify, and redistribute the Software and Modified Software, in source or
executable form, and to operate it as a hosted service. No ownership transfers.
Rights not expressly granted are reserved.

3. Mandatory commercial license above USD 20,000 per month

A company whose Monthly Revenue exceeds USD 20,000 must request AND obtain
a separate written commercial Savia license from Licensor before exercising
any of the rights granted in section 2. Submitting a request does not grant
permission. This requirement applies to internal use, development, testing,
production, hosted services, and redistribution, including through contractors.
An individual may not rely on personal eligibility to operate the Software
for a company that exceeds the threshold.

For ongoing eligibility, assess both the immediately preceding calendar month
and revenue accumulated in the current calendar month. If either exceeds
USD 20,000, a commercial license is required. A new company with no preceding
month assesses the current month. Exactly USD 20,000 does not exceed the
threshold. If You cross the threshold while using the Software, stop exercising
the licensed rights until a commercial license is effective. Earlier compliant
use is not retroactively made a breach by later revenue growth.

Commercial pricing and additional terms are agreed separately with Licensor.
A commercial license does not waive source-publication or attribution duties
unless its written terms expressly do so. Request commercial terms from
Hefesoft SAS through the official Savia repository's maintainer contact channel:
https://github.com/hefesoftsas/savia
Do not publish confidential revenue information in a public issue.

4. Redistribution and publication of modifications

Whenever You distribute the Software or Modified Software to another person
or entity, whether for payment or free of charge, You must:

(a) Include this License and the NOTICE file, preserve copyright, licensing,
    attribution, and third-party notices, and identify Your modifications and
    their dates without representing them as authored or endorsed by Licensor.
(b) License the covered Software, including Your modifications, to recipients
    under this same License. Each recipient remains subject to section 3.
    You may not add restrictions that prevent exercise of these rights.
(c) Make the complete corresponding source of the distributed version publicly
    available at no charge, without registration, under this License, no later
    than the first distribution. This includes all modifications and the build,
    installation, and configuration scripts needed to reproduce that version.
    A patch alone is insufficient unless the exact base source is also available.
(d) Supply a clearly identified source URL with each distribution and in the
    application's legal or about page. Keep that exact version available for
    at least three years after Your last distribution of that version, and
    publish the source of every subsequent modified release You distribute.

Private modifications need not be published until distributed. Network access
to a hosted instance alone is not distribution for this section; the revenue
and visible-attribution requirements still apply to hosted instances. Business
records, user data, passwords, private keys, and production secrets are not
corresponding source and must not be included. Independently authored works
that merely communicate with Savia through an API are not automatically
Modified Software. Third-party dependencies retain their own licenses.

5. Mandatory visible attribution

Every original or modified deployment and distribution must clearly identify
the product as Savia and display the following notice:

    Savia — Desarrollado por Hefesoft SAS, Colombia.

An English equivalent may be displayed in addition:

    Savia — Developed by Hefesoft SAS, Colombia.

For graphical and web interfaces, the required notice must remain legible and
visible during normal use, including on login and public-facing pages, in a
persistent footer, header, or equivalent area. An about page, source comment,
or hidden legal link alone is insufficient. Responsive layouts must preserve
readable attribution. For command-line programs, show it at startup and in
help/version output. For headless APIs or MCP services with no user interface,
include it in service-identification metadata and public documentation. Include
it in distributed documentation and product descriptions as well.

You may add Your own branding and authorship notices for Your contributions,
but may not remove, hide, obscure, or replace the Savia attribution. This
License permits use of the Savia and Hefesoft names to fulfill these duties;
it does not otherwise grant trademark rights or permission to imply endorsement.

