7. Termination

Your rights under this License terminate automatically upon a breach. Except
for commercial eligibility under section 3, rights are reinstated if You cure
the breach within 30 days after first becoming aware of it, provided Licensor
has not previously terminated Your rights for a breach. Reinstatement does not
excuse liability for a breach. Revenue-based ineligibility is resolved only by
obtaining a commercial license or again satisfying section 3; there is no
30-day permission to operate above the threshold. Compliant recipients retain
their own rights. Sections concerning notices on retained copies, third-party
rights, disclaimers, liability, and interpretation survive termination.

